# Everything in this directory is written by scripts/stamp-revision.sh before each generate/build and
# is deliberately NOT committed. The stamp holds the build commit's short hash, and a commit's hash is
# a function of its own contents, so a committed hash could only ever be a PREVIOUS commit's —
# permanently stale, which is the exact failure the diagnostics build-provenance stamp exists to avoid.
#
# This file is committed for two reasons beyond documenting that: it makes the directory exist in a
# fresh clone (the recursive `ios/faBolus` source path picks up whatever XcodeGen finds here, and git
# cannot track an empty directory), and it makes an accidental `git add` of the generated file
# impossible without an explicit -f.
*
!.gitignore
